<% content_for :title, "Demos — yrby" %>

<section>
  <h1>Demos</h1>
  <p>
    Every demo runs on one <code>DocumentChannel</code>. The server never looks
    inside the document; it records the CRDT update, acks it, and relays it. What
    changes from page to page is only the Yjs shape the browser binds to.
  </p>
  <p class="warning">
    Rooms are public and temporary. Opening a demo puts you in a room of your
    own; share the URL to collaborate. Anyone with the link can edit, and a
    room untouched for 24 hours is deleted.
  </p>

  <ul class="demo-list">
    <% @demos.each do |demo| %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to demo.title, demo_path(demo.slug) %>
        <code><%= demo.shape %></code>
        <span><%= demo.blurb %></span>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>
